@flexiarg snatch/institutions-vary-by-position-and-force
@title Institutions Vary by Position and Force
@audience institution designers, vocabulary authors
@tone foundational
@style pattern
@how snatch/preserve-the-right-to-abstain snatch/mark-without-force snatch/revert-then-invert snatch/non-binding-talk-still-moves-play

! conclusion: Place each arrangement by where it intervenes in the interaction and with what force, rather than listing arrangements.

  + context: Snatch or Share holds one core interaction fixed across five
    treatments — P1 abstains or offers (give X, ask A); P2 accepts, refuses or
    snatches — and varies only what is added around it.

  + IF:
    You must design, compare, or extend a family of institutional arrangements.

  + HOWEVER:
    A list of arrangements shows its members and not its gaps: nothing in a list
    says what two entries share, or what is missing between them.

  + THEN:
    Place each arrangement on two axes — **where** it intervenes (before the
    choice / at the choice set / after the outcome) and **with what force**
    (none / symbolic / material) — and read the family off the grid.

  + BECAUSE:
    A family placed on axes exhibits its own gaps and lets a new member be
    derived rather than invented. Growth by adding entries to a list cannot say
    whether the new entry is a distinction or a duplicate.
    + evidence: the five treatments occupy five cells and no two coincide —
      G1 baseline (no intervention); G2 at the choice set, material (an option is
      removed); G3 after the outcome, symbolic (a mark, no payoff change);
      G4 after the outcome, material (revert plus inverse transfer); G5 before
      the choice, none (a non-binding channel). The grid also shows what is
      absent: nothing intervenes before the choice with material force, and
      nothing intervenes at the choice set symbolically.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - Read any existing vocabulary of arrangements against these axes and ask
      which cells are occupied by more than one entry, and which by none.
